'''Xenobeast Bunaglios''' (超拳獣ブンナグリオス, ''Chō Kenjū Bunnaguriosu'', '''Super Fist-Beast Bunnaglios''') is an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of [[Teacher Bun Bun]] that appears in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Hunt for the Xenobeast]]. He was added in [[Version 14.1 Update|Version 14.1]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Xenobeast Bunaglios
|image = E 714.png
|appearance = [[Hunt for the Xenobeast]]
|money drop = 5,050¢ - 19,947¢
}}

==Enemy==
This explosive titan is very unique for a [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variant, as he has a slower attack rate, lower DPS, and a longer foreswing compared to every other Bun Bun, in exchange for health surpassing [[Relic Bun-Bun]], very high damage per hit, and an unusually long 400 range. His heavy damage is augmented by a guaranteed [[Explosion]] and an Omni Strike with enough reach to hit most backliners, which together can extend his maximum reach to 675 while dramatically increasing his effective damage output. He also possesses a 20% chance for a [[Critical Hit]] (which is translated to his Explosion if the initial hit is a Crit), up to doubling his already high damage and particularly threatening the use of [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]]. Finally, he is immune to Freeze and Knockback, meaning cats like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]] will be useless against this enemy. While Bunnaglios is relatively easy to fight on his own due to how many counters exist, especially [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]], almost every stage he appears in features deadly support that can kill Soap Cat and other [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien units]] easily.

Note that unlike most other Bun Buns, Xenobeast Bunaglios is not a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy, despite visually flying and floating.

==Strategy==
Although Xenobeast Bunaglios loses the Floating typing to reduce the number of viable counters against him, his Behemoth type can be exploited by using [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayers]] to deal more damage and soak up hits, provided they can get in range. [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] is as an extremely potent counter thanks to being Resistant to Aliens, having Behemoth Slayer to further reduce damage, and being able to Weaken Bunaglios to tank for even longer, but will have to watch out for other enemies. [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] can also tank Bunaglios' attacks and hold its ground, albeit being more reliant on Dodging. It's ill-advised to use [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] as your tanker as Bunaglios' Critical Hits will instantly kill him.

