==Trivia==
*The 'Xeno' in Xenobeast comes from the Greek word ''xenos'', meaning 'foreign' or 'foreigner.'
*Based on his Japanese name (ブンナグリオス ''Bunnaguriosu''), Bunaglios is likely derived from ''[[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Bun]]'' and ぶん殴り ''bunnaguri'' (continuative of ぶん殴る ''bunnaguru'', "to violently beat up"). His English name being Bunaglios rather than Bunnagurios or Bunnagrios appears to be a misromanization similar to [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil|Deonil]].
*Given the "ios" in his name, explosive punching abilities, and overall design (particularly his blue coloration, fists and tail), Bunaglios' ''Monster Hunter'' reference is likely [[wikia:monsterhunter:Brachydios|Brachydios]], which uses a symbiotic slime mold to spread volatile slime and give its punches explosive impact. His high status and darker color scheme suggest that he may specifically be based on [[wikia:monsterhunter:Raging Brachydios|Raging Brachydios]], its more explosive and violent variant.
**Bunaglios' color scheme, horns, tail and [[Explosion]]s may also have some influence from ''Monster Hunter Rise: Sunbreak''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s final boss, the Devil-inspired [[:Wikia:monsterhunter:Gaismagorm|Gaismagorm]], as befits a Great [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]]. The Bun Buns already look somewhat demonic to begin with, and Bunaglios' loss of [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait and change of habitat are reminiscent of the ''Archdemon Wingtalon'' material's description, which says it has "no hint of the divine heights [Gaismagorm] once knew," implying the Gaismagorm species was once able to fly until they came to thrive underground. Gaismagorm is often called the "Archdemon of the Abyss", which may fit into a potential theme of the Great Advent Bosses, powerful demons: [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]]'s Japanese title is 大魔王 ''Daimaō'' ("Great Demon King"), while [[Kappy Kawano]] is a possible reference to Sally's father from [[wikipedia:Sally the Witch|''Sally the Witch'']], [http://stat.ameba.jp/user_images/20160617/20/yoko5137/a2/f8/j/o0480084413675182605.jpg Mr. Yumeno], also known as the 魔王 ''Maō'' ("Demon King").
**The phrases "Monstrous Teacher" and "The hunt is on!" in [[Hunt for the Xenobeast]]'s [[Media:Eve l 169 en.png|event poster]] likely allude to Bunaglios being inspired by ''Monster Hunter''.
*Since most of the other Advent Bosses appear to have religious inspirations, Bunaglios may represent Lucifer, given his demon-like appearance, banishment to the wild, loss of Floating trait, the hellish background of [[King of the Beasts: Final Bout (Brutal)|King of the Beasts: Final Bout]], and how he became a feared, high-ranking figure in the place he was exiled to, mirroring Lucifer's fall from Heaven. The name Lucifer means "light-bearer" or "light-bringer" and originally referred to the "morning star", the planet Venus as it appears at dawn, which may have inspired Bunaglios' glowing fists and horns and [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] trait. His Explosion ability may be related to how Hell is associated with [[wikipedia:Sulfur|sulfur]], a component in gunpowder, which Lucifer creates in ''[[wikipedia:Paradise Lost|Paradise Lost]]''.
**As king of all wild beasts, Bunaglios could also represent the angel of the abyss, [[wikipedia:Abaddon|Abaddon]], who is king of an army of locusts. Abaddon is known as "Destroyer" and outright means "destruction" in Hebrew, which fits with Bunaglios' destructive Explosions. Like Lucifer, Abaddon is sometimes interpreted as the Devil himself.
**Either of these references is supported by Bunaglios' possible inspiration from Gaismagorm, which also takes after both Lucifer and Abaddon.
*"King of all wild beasts" is an accurate translation of 百獣の王 ''hyakujū no ō'', which can literally be taken as "king of a hundred beasts", but is actually an idiom most commonly used in reference to the lion, king of the animal kingdom. Although 百獣 consists of the kanji for "hundred" (百) and "beast" (獣), this compound word normally doesn't refer to exactly a hundred beasts, but to all or many kinds of beasts/animals.
*Xenobeast Bunaglios can be seen as a foil to Infernal Tyrant Nyandam. Both are blue, four-horned, knockback-immune Great Advent Boss variants of [[Empire of Cats]] [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon/Iriomote]] bosses with 400 range and hand-based attacks, but Nyandam is darker, attacks with hands made of darkness, and voluntarily took his current form for a marriage photo shoot, while Bunaglios is lighter, attacks with a hand that radiates light, and wound up in the wild against his will.
*Xenobeast Bunaglios is the first Advent Boss to have a non-standard enemy type, that being [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]].
**He is also the first Advent Boss variant of [[Teacher Bun Bun]], while [[The Face]] and [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] both already had three each (counting [[Evil Emperor Cat]] and [[Possessed Empress]] as Nyandam variants).
*His Explosion ability may be intended as an upgrade to [[Bun Bun Symbiote]]'s level 1 [[Wave Attack]].

